      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day, and the usual single-dose maximum is 800 mg. A dose that high carries serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a transcription or unit error. For example, the intended order might be 1600 mg total per day (400 mg four times daily), or 800 mg three times daily (2,400 mg/day).\n\nAlso, medication orders normally come from a licensed prescriber who is treating the patient. If the treating clinician wants this order, they should confirm the intended dose with me or enter it themselves.\n\nIf you send me a corrected dose from the prescriber, I'll enter it right away. One example is ibuprofen 400 mg or 800 mg by mouth with food, at a set frequency."
      }
