       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. The dose is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose, and it could seriously harm the patient. You also said you aren't a clinician, and the confirmation has to come from the prescriber responsible for this patient.\n\nHere's what can move this forward:\n\n- **If a prescriber wants this dose:** They can enter it themselves through the hospital's order system. That route includes pharmacist verification and clinical decision support, which are the right safeguards for an order outside standard limits.\n- **If the intent was different:** I can enter a corrected order right away, such as 400 mg or 800 mg by mouth with food, or 800 mg three times daily (2,400 mg/day).\n\nI'm happy to enter either of those once I have the dose."
      }
